Z||000000||hugh||03-06-2001||08:07 PM||||Headline <BR>On the front page of our local paper.<BR>     S.J.SPARED WORST OF STORM<P>   As a story on the side of the page<BR>      2 die 13 hurt in shooting at CALIF. school<P>       IS SOMETHING WRONG WITH THIS PICTURE?<P>   I don't know how to feel about this.I feel the children's story is more important than a story on the weather,even though the weather impacts more people.I don't want to see more on it,I just want it to be more important than the weather.Are we too used to it?Would more publicity contribute to copycat incidents?As I said I don't know how to feel. ||||reg||9
Z||000001||pHoOl||03-06-2001||09:26 PM||||I have noticed that our local news stations tend to make a big deal about the weather over different stories.  However, i think that part of the reason that these school shootings are getting popular (despite the fact that the rates are going down) are from media coverage.  After every one of these events, there are schools around the nation who have copy cats that make fake bomb threats trying to get out of school.  They play off the fact that it is so shocking.<P><BR>I don't, however, have an idea of what to do about it, so i won't pretend that i do.  <P><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Galen||03-07-2001||12:55 AM||||I'll admit that a school shooting is probably a big deal, but can we get to the root of the problem here? the media makes a HUGE deal out of it, causing more problems. Okie, two students are dead, yes I feel bad for the students, the kids families, friends and the such. Okie, done. We dont need to know whats going on every second there. <P>"So what if I'm cold hearted, atleast I have a heart."||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||03-07-2001||02:20 PM||||This is why I don't watch news... It's mostly just a downer.  People are dying every second of every day.  When was the last time you saw the birth of a child on the front page?  People don't want to see that.  They want to see celebrities on their newspapers and Tommy Hilfiger on their underwear.||||reg||1
